# This project does not read secrets from environment variables. Every
# credential it needs lives in a gitignored *file*, not a .env value:
#
#   credentials.json   Gmail OAuth client secret, downloaded once from Google
#                       Cloud Console (Appendix Alef). Never committed; see
#                       .gitignore.
#   token.json          Written by the one-time Gmail consent flow the first
#                       time [email] is enabled in game.toml. Never committed.
#   ~/.config/ngrok/ngrok.yml
#                       ngrok's own authtoken, written by
#                       `ngrok config add-authtoken <token>` run once in your
#                       own terminal. This repository never reads or holds it.
#
# This file exists to satisfy the "config separate from code" guideline and to
# document that boundary explicitly, since there is no secret-bearing env var
# to place a placeholder for.
#
# The only environment variables the code ever touches are non-secret Tk
# library path overrides on Windows (src/police_agent/gui/__init__.py), and
# only when the interpreter cannot already find them:
#
# TCL_LIBRARY=
# TK_LIBRARY=
